{"title":"2003 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(x_as_smallest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (x as smallest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(x_as_largest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (x as largest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(x_as_middle_number)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (x as middle number)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Official_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Official Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <i>sum of the squares</i> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive positive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e5e6c1abc9d9aac7e48a58c29b99f1b91009bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest of these integers?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28x_as_smallest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(x_as_smallest)\">Solution 1 (x as smallest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (x as smallest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest integer of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. Since the numbers are five consecutive positive integers, the numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edc688e33895bf81c1b912055950d33a03e375a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, x + 1, x + 2, x + 3, x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of the squares of these numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e5e6c1abc9d9aac7e48a58c29b99f1b91009bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19bd0600edb9843c7dff480f22d2ad5c3a5c989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + (x + 1)^{2} + (x + 2)^{2} + (x + 3)^{2} + (x + 4)^{2} = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"422\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/85089169964a3a59a8e85a75741e2242db2bd627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + x^{2} + 2 \\times 1 \\times x + 1^{2} + x^{2} + 2 \\times 2 \\times x + 2^{2} + x^{2} + 2 \\times 3 \\times x + 3^{2} + x^{2} + 4 \\times 2 \\times x + 4^{2} = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"777\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c707acfb02674bbf4176c66851b090fc7faa57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 2x + 1 + 4x + 4 + 6x + 9 + 8x + 16 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"391\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808f864807b39a4de73a1d2737e77ec7c98b790a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 20x + 30 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since all of the coefficients end in either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to make this equation easier to solve:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d4c084c838ac36e647ee91656c8ca5367389e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x^{2} + 20x + 30}{5} = \\frac{1815}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8be48b40c1eb43e881ab1eaaf347d1aa67ca7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x + 6 = 363$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/094f8227369029f7db170f0d24d7987825923651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x + 6 - 363 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f2a1c2e0383095ac78d3b4af06420f7622e700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x - 357 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa092fdebf473c16959c371c43f6c2804964febe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$357 = 17 \\times 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart, so this is equivalent to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bdb8500f6a56bc4a6c89b59bde24a1138f160af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 21x - 17x - 357 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230ff5d0e76277916725e6f0c4d6e550dba00b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 21) - 17(x + 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac169e25ac93fb0b4491c45b895fea9b2c8658c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 17)(x + 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/0068c5ec3d3c48dff57ad14ad4e0eaa8569f4e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 17 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444f84a733ebd2e1a8aba7055b84b112b9c9a5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 21 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />, as the only way to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as a product here is if at least one of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4e706959c6ef3bcaecc3e541404598c8cf3bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0ac3a850d13c5efe3f2c50faf65c639541d507e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4e706959c6ef3bcaecc3e541404598c8cf3bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. We could have also seen this through the quadratic formula.\n</p><p>The largest of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b4c3e97b90e7ed8f39e9634f062b3abc343052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/4113a57eeae04af75d2ed689a9fc084638a550c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 4 = \\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28x_as_largest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(x_as_largest)\">Solution 2 (x as largest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (x as largest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the largest integer of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. Since the numbers are five consecutive positive integers, the numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b2293d2c25c7a4f889a3e175db3232b5f935d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 4, x - 3, x - 2, x - 1, x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of the squares of these numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e5e6c1abc9d9aac7e48a58c29b99f1b91009bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38799d4cd23d7003ebf1b963c2ad37f343e1bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 4)^{2} + (x - 3)^{2} + (x - 2)^{2} + (x - 1)^{2} + x^{2} = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"422\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168dd46b2f993317d5a3fc9ac8d3afea8b4c689a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 2 \\times 4 \\times x + 4^{2} + x^{3} - 2 \\times 3 \\times x + 3^{2} + x^{2} - 2 \\times 2 \\times x + 2^{2} + x^{2} - 2 \\times 1 \\times x + 1^{2} + x^{2} = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"777\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e61953ae1d661b43cbf12deb69e45de56d6464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} - 8x + 1 - 6x + 4 - 4x + 9 - 2x + 16 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"391\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e904c02b13744c321a723ea1beccbdaf16162f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} - 20x + 30 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since all of the coefficients end in either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to make this equation easier to solve:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca21b90c5998f535dce487e98cedd6c8df1a1c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x^{2} - 20x + 30}{5} = \\frac{1815}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2bc026bd795054387998c8468185cd2dfee331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 4x + 6 = 363$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70d2ec36d262edb99b72425c833e3f91fc2e7cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 4x + 6 - 363 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785a457eea47b468aff7a0c97ad4ebe7080785e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 4x - 357 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa092fdebf473c16959c371c43f6c2804964febe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$357 = 17 \\times 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart, so this is equivalent to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9fe02ab5938dc0c6d5e53bf4db584f40092975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 21x + 17x - 357 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6ad24a8ac4b0880162a63cd4155d0e184f4bc33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x +-21) + 17(x - 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2edb77e72bdbc65cc995338ff69f49c6a5148bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + 17)(x - 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367ed45b9bd6d1f5c4e7103e391f65ec029d5e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 17 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/24123d268d5eb41d5af6009a05d75fa7a556527c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 21 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />, as the only way to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as a product here is if at least one of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ead88fe219f724f8dab5687c7a160c7ca2f4ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3cd57dcf1fe1c4d142904c4e6413c30e2dfec5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6abb0fbf47cc109c2a4005c502b585778c441dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28x_as_middle_number.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(x_as_middle_number)\">Solution 3 (x as middle number)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (x as middle number)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the median of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. Since the numbers are five consecutive positive integers, the numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c9949649dedfa621605bcf9854b4475353b58858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2, x - 1, x, x + 1, x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of the squares of these numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e5e6c1abc9d9aac7e48a58c29b99f1b91009bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/5663c3152a29a1f29ff347824bcbf6c536ba5d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 2)^{2} + (x - 1)^{2} + x^{2} + (x + 1)^{2} + (x + 2)^{2} = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"422\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b78589cedb199cd109971e81d12f1ca887b4d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 2 \\times 2 \\times x + 2^{2} + x^{2} - 2 \\times 1 \\times x + x^{2} + x^{2} + 2 \\times 1 \\times x + 1^{2} + x^{2} + 2 \\times 2 \\times x + 2^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"677\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> term will just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when adding everything up, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb1001eb49106b8f26950c909d4ba9f82055e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 4 + 1 + 1 + 4 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/70846c20437e96387a85ffc32dd5549ec2f0d351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 10 = 1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since all of the coefficients of these terms end in either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1588cada2d1b39707e82c199fd0baa7034c41fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x^{2} + 10}{5} = \\frac{1815}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e741aa4c39b40e206a606ed2e84e59eb08a2582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 2 = 363$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00a014f32429ec34cabcaf2b5efe97f04bfa66d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} = 363 - 2 = 361$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/4608b883d6390beddf07df17ac9e032074d036cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm \\sqrt{361}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"21\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd68e293deb6caeab718e1ade01dfc23aebf3c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{361} = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The largest integer of the five numbers was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28829eb053db1b3885e9d5380c4be3744f4846d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 = 19 + 2 = \\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"171\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Official_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Official_Solution_1)\">Solution 4 (Official Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Official Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the sum of the squares of the consecutive numbers was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e5e6c1abc9d9aac7e48a58c29b99f1b91009bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, the square of the middle number of the five consecutive numbers should be close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61e54bd1e7ab70de2c8adc6c595ac1a811b13cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1815}{5} = 363$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b5ef94cf6fbb9494eab6efae61a399408cc6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19^{2} = 361$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />, so the middle number should be about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This would then make the largest number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4f6233fd29613567202bd47d497c7c5b8df16d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 + 2 = \\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher and CEMC\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202315\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 439/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16370/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.998      1 2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    5.998      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36911:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202315 and revision id 285697. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}